          "text": "{\"locale\":\"en\",\"claims\":[{\"text\":\"Maintenance is distinguished from repair by its earlier focus: it addresses the consequences produced by ongoing operation while a system can still function, asking whether its supporting conditions are gradually changing.\",\"supportFragmentIds\":[\"F-0b99d2d8edfe06d9c771891ea3d36420a8ee77a5456a9b98fda2407489166a9b98fda2407489166a9f\"]},{\"text\":\"Repair usually occurs after a structure has already been clearly damaged; maintenance is therefore not simply repair performed earlier.\",\"supportFragmentIds\":[\"F-0b99d2d8edfe06d9c771891ea3d36420a8ee77a5456a9b98fda2407489166a9f\"]}],\"sourceLanguages\":[\"zh-Hans\"],\"status\":\"supported\",\"boundary\":\"The fragment supports this conceptual timing and focus distinction only. It does not specify particular maintenance actions, damage thresholds, or component-replacement conditions.\"}"
